 about the problem.

We need to generate a high-quality training dataset for DFlash (block-diffusion speculative decoding) to create a small ~0.8B draft model that can be used with the 754B-parameter GLM-5.1 MoE teacher (Zhipu AI).

Key requirements for the DFlash dataset (per the 2026 paper):
- 50K–800K sequences (start with 50K–100K for PoC, scale to 200K–400K for good quality).
- Each sequence: packed short examples (initially 64–128 tokens) into longer contexts (target 4K–16K token windows).
- For every sequence we must extract:
  - Generated tokens from the teacher.
  - Hidden-layer context vectors from exactly 5 uniformly sampled layers (between layer 2 and third-to-last).
  - 512 random anchor positions per sequence for block-diffusion training.
  - Top-K or full next-token distributions (optional but useful).

Core compute challenge:
- Full GLM-5.1 model (quantized with Unsloth UD-Q2_K_XL) is 205 GB total:
  - 15 GB dense layers.
  - 190 GB MoE experts.
- Even on a high-memory Colab TPUv6 instance (~173 GB system RAM / 225 GB disk), the full model cannot be loaded at once for efficient inference.
- Naïve full-model loading + batched prefill is SSD-bound and extremely slow for the required dataset size.
- We must support layer-wise expert deduplication (only load active experts per token) and selective hidden-state extraction to avoid materializing massive activations/KV caches.
- Without a smart sharding + streaming strategy, dataset generation becomes impractical on consumer/cloud TPUs and would require a full cluster.

2. Proposed Solution / Way We Want to Address It
We will implement layer-wise, pipeline-parallel inference on TPUs using the Unsloth UD-Q2_K_XL weights. The model will be split into two halves so that each half (approximately half the layers) fits comfortably inside a single 32 GB TPU slice.

High-Level Workflow
- Offline dataset preparation (this phase):
  - Start with curated short sequences (64–128 tokens) from high-quality sources (e.g., Nemotron Post-Training Dataset V2 + code/data mixtures).
